================================================================================
py4DSTEM (conventions)
================================================================================

The apps' lattice convention (a along x, b in the xy plane; reciprocal vectors
without 2 pi; structure factors in A) follows py4DSTEM's Crystal class
(py4DSTEM/process/diffraction/crystal.py). No py4DSTEM code is in slice 1; the
Lobato & Van Dyck scattering table of slice 2 will be py4DSTEM's.

    py4DSTEM - https://github.com/py4dstem/py4DSTEM
    Copyright (C) The py4DSTEM developers
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License v3.0

================================================================================
pymatgen (the oracle of slice 1; no code copied)
================================================================================

Cells, expanded CIF sites, symmetry operations (spglib behind pymatgen),
d-spacings and the reflections within a sphere are checked against pymatgen
2026.9.24 / pymatgen-core 2026.9.23 by tools/slice-1/pins.py, whose output is
the committed fixture slice-1-pins.json. The Laue orbit and the absence rule are
computed from pymatgen's operations by the registration's definitions, in NumPy.

